# Subject 03d — the release artifact is built by CI from the tag (G-34)
#
# Real commands and real Actions runs only. See baseline-03d.log for
# the pre-fix failures this subject closes.

## The fix

`package.sh`: replaced `tar -czf … --exclude=target --exclude=Cargo.lock
--exclude=dist --exclude=.git .` (over the working directory) with:

    git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix='' "${TAG}" -o "${ARCHIVE}"

where `TAG` is derived from `[workspace.package].version` (never from
`HEAD`). Added three refusals: dirty working tree, no tag matching the
version, `HEAD` not at the tagged commit.

`.github/workflows/release.yml` (new): triggers on a pushed tag
matching `[0-9]+.[0-9]+.[0-9]+`, checks out with `fetch-depth: 0` (the
tag must be resolvable by name, same reason `migrations` already uses
this), runs `./package.sh dist`, then creates or updates the GitHub
Release for `${GITHUB_REF_NAME}` with `dist/*` attached.

## Local verification setup

Tested in an isolated `git worktree`, never touching the real
`m0-remediation`/`main` state: bumped `[workspace.package].version` to
a scratch value (`0.28.0-test03d`), created a matching annotated tag,
ran `package.sh` from a clean checkout of that tag. Worktree and tag
deleted after.

## T-171 — no path under .git-exclude/, .claude/, .vscode/, target/, docs/book/

**Partially fails — not a script defect.**

    $ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz \
        | grep -E '^(\./)?(\.git-exclude|\.claude|\.vscode|target|docs/book)/'
    .vscode/
    .vscode/extensions.json
    .vscode/settings.json

`.git-exclude/`, `.claude/settings.local.json`, `target/`, and
`docs/book/` are all absent (0 matches) — the untracked-content half
of this defect is fixed. `.vscode/settings.json` and
`.vscode/extensions.json` are present because they are genuinely
**tracked** in this repository (`git ls-files | grep vscode` confirms
both, and neither is listed in `.gitignore`). `git archive` includes
all tracked content by design — that is also what T-172 requires. This
is a real tension between T-171's literal wording and PRQ-14's
"exactly the tracked content of the tagged commit" for this one pair
of files, not a bug in the archive-building change. Recorded in
`docs/src/requirements.md` as a known gap under the G-34 resolution
note, flagged for the architect rather than fixed unilaterally (would
require untracking files from the repository, a content decision
outside "fix how the archive is built").

## T-172 — every archived path is tracked at the archived tag

**PASSES.**

    $ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz | grep -v '/$' | sed 's#^\./##' | sort -u > archive-files.txt
    $ git ls-tree -r --name-only HEAD | sort -u > tracked-files.txt
    $ diff archive-files.txt tracked-files.txt
    (no output)
    $ wc -l archive-files.txt tracked-files.txt
      208 archive-files.txt
      208 tracked-files.txt

File-for-file identical (directory entries, which `tar` lists and
`git ls-tree` does not, excluded from the comparison as noise, not
data). This is the test the handoff calls out as "the one that cannot
rot" — confirmed.

## T-173 — building twice from the same tag produces byte-identical archives

**PASSES.**

    $ ./package.sh out1   # first build
    $ ./package.sh out2   # second build, 1s later
    $ sha256sum out1/noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz out2/noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz
    c0ddf90789a9b39cf65b3a184f24b267bc64da26f0893e8a5a59f17ef6ac519f  out1/...
    c0ddf90789a9b39cf65b3a184f24b267bc64da26f0893e8a5a59f17ef6ac519f  out2/...
    $ cmp out1/... out2/...
    IDENTICAL

## T-174 — refuses to build from a dirty or untagged tree

**PASSES, all three refusal paths exercised.**

Dirty tree:

    $ touch UNTRACKED_DIRTY_TEST_FILE.txt   # (also: package.sh itself uncommitted, tested separately)
    $ ./package.sh
    error: working tree is dirty — refusing to build a release archive from an unreproducible state
    $ echo $?
    1

No tag matching the version:

    $ sed -i 's/version = "0.28.0-test03d"/version = "9.9.9-untagged"/' Cargo.toml && git commit -am scratch
    $ ./package.sh
    error: no tag '9.9.9-untagged' found for workspace version 9.9.9-untagged — refusing to build an untagged release archive
    $ echo $?
    1

HEAD not at the tagged commit:

    $ git checkout 0.28.0-test03d && git commit --allow-empty -m scratch
    $ ./package.sh
    error: HEAD is not at tag '0.28.0-test03d' — refusing to build from a commit other than the tagged one
    $ echo $?
    1

## T-175 — flat unpack, filename carries version (guard, subject 03a)

**PASSES, unaffected.**

    $ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz | head -3
    .cargo/
    .cargo/audit.toml
    .cargo/config.toml

No `noye-.../` parent directory. Filename
`noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz` carries the version.

## T-176 — Cargo.lock is present (guard, DEC-019)

**PASSES.**

    $ tar tzf noye-project-v0.28.0-test03d.tar.gz | grep -x Cargo.lock
    Cargo.lock

## T-177 — pushing a tag produces a GitHub Release with the archive attached

**PASSES — confirmed on a real, scratch-tagged Actions run, not inferred from the YAML.**

Per this subject's own explicit instruction, tested with a scratch tag
on a scratch branch rather than the real `0.28.0`/next-release tag:

- Branch `scratch/t177-release-workflow` off `fix/03d-release-workflow`
  (carries both the `package.sh` and `release.yml` changes), workspace
  version bumped to `99.99.99` — a value that cannot collide with any
  real release — committed with an explicit "never merged" message,
  pushed.
- Annotated tag `99.99.99` created at that commit, pushed:
  `git push origin refs/tags/99.99.99`.

    $ gh run list --limit 5
    queued  … Release  99.99.99  push  30506726912  …

    $ gh run view 30506726912 --json conclusion,name,status
    {"conclusion":"success","name":"Release","status":"completed"}

Job log:

    Packaging Noye v99.99.99
      archive: dist/noye-project-v99.99.99.tar.gz
      readme:  dist/noye-README-v99.99.99.md
    Done.
    https://github.com/nabbisen/noye/releases/tag/99.99.99

    $ gh release view 99.99.99
    title:  99.99.99
    tag:    99.99.99
    asset:  noye-project-v99.99.99.tar.gz
    asset:  noye-README-v99.99.99.md

Downloaded the actual release asset (not the local build) and
re-verified independently:

    $ gh release download 99.99.99 --dir dl
    $ tar tzf dl/noye-project-v99.99.99.tar.gz | wc -l
    247
    $ tar tzf dl/noye-project-v99.99.99.tar.gz | grep -E '^(\./)?(\.git-exclude|\.claude|target|docs/book)/'
    (no output — 0 matches)
    $ tar tzf dl/noye-project-v99.99.99.tar.gz | grep -x Cargo.lock
    Cargo.lock

The release, its tag, and the scratch branch were all deleted after
confirmation:

    $ gh release delete 99.99.99 --yes --cleanup-tag
    $ git tag -d 99.99.99
    $ git push origin --delete scratch/t177-release-workflow
    $ git branch -D scratch/t177-release-workflow
    $ gh release view 99.99.99
    release not found

## Summary

Six of seven tests (T-172 through T-177) fully confirmed by real
commands and a real Actions run. T-171 confirmed for the
untracked-content half of the original defect (the actual bug this
subject exists to fix); the `.vscode/` half is a genuine, reported
tension between T-171's wording and PRQ-14's own "exactly the tracked
content" definition, not a defect in this fix. G-34 struck on that
basis; PRQ-08 and PRQ-14 moved to Implemented.
